workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/delegate-invocation-reference.md) for the exact architect sign-off protocol.\nReading the archived Phase 2 architect sign-off prompt and findings ([1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase2-signoff.prompt.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/archive/dao-space-query/1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase2-signoff.prompt.md) and [1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase2-signoff.gemini-4-argon.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/archive/dao-space-query/1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase2-signoff.gemini-4-argon.findings.md)), along with the full `git diff master..datomic-q-p3-ci`.\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-26 14:29:02 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-26 21:29:02 +07\nCoding-Agent: agy\nSession-ID: 19a3d247-adc0-4f98-9d2b-e03cd1c5f3f5\n\n# Lead System Architect Sign-Off Review — `dao.space.query.datomic` Phase 3 (`164da9c0f`)\n\n**Reviewed Range**: `master...datomic-q-p3-ci` (`8f31f8f23..164da9c0f`, 10 files changed, `+699/-67`; disjoint from `8f31f8f23..master` at `671cd21f4`).\n**Method**: Read-only static and mathematical audit of the full diff, evaluator kernel, adapter boundary, errata, conformance corpus (`113` cases: `56` executable, `9` difference, `19` refusal, `29` pending; `28` points; `12` fixtures verified via Python JSON inspection), and the Jolt J2 applicability manifest ([jolt_j2_lane.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj)). (Host JVM/Chez execution under `~/.local` is blocked in headless `--mode plan --sandbox`, per [delegate-invocation-reference.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/delegate-invocation-reference.md#L280-L292); jupiter three-host and downstream gates are evaluated as orchestrator/reviewer evidence.)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Tabling Fixed-Point Completeness vs. r3-Era Kernel Requirements\n\n**Sound in core Bekić fixed-point structure, kernel state-threading, demand, and budget backstop — EXCEPT for one missed P1 completeness defect (`::hits` key collision across concurrent leader activations; see Question 4, D1).**\n\n- **Single kernel, lexical scope vs. invocation progress, constant stack**:\n  - [`emit-rule`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2086-L2110), [`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2057-L2083), [`rule-iteration`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2011-L2055), and [`read-table`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1995-L2008) run on the shared `[state result]` trampoline (`bounce` / `bind` / `each-st`) with zero atoms, volatiles, or dynamic vars.\n  - `::tables` is scoped lexically to `body-ctx` ([query.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2016)), leaving caller `ctx` untouched on return while threading `st` forward across passes, definitions, and sibling branches — honoring the r3 ruling ([1792862294000-architect-datomic-q-phase4-stop-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/archive/dao-space-query/1792862294000-architect-datomic-q-phase4-stop-r3.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L54-L63)).\n  - Call keys `[rule-name (binding-key arg-vals)]` and tuple deduplication `(binding-key tuple)` preserve CBOR content-strict numeric identity (`1` vs. `1.0`, `1.0M` vs. `1.00M`, `+0.0` vs. `-0.0`), and `:seen` / `:new` update before [`unify-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2047-L2048) so repeated call-site variables like `(path ?x ?x)` retain off-diagonal intermediate tuples in the table across passes.\n  - First-witness existential demand (`not` / `not-join` via [`exists-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1878-L1885)) short-circuits mid-pass through `reduced`, and every pass that re-enters a table charges at least `:rule-entry` (plus `:candidate` per tabled tuple), guaranteeing structured `:step-budget-exhausted` termination on fresh-value divergence.\n- **Why single-call left/right/both/mutual recursion converges (Bekić's theorem), and where multi-call conjunctions break (D1)**:\n  - For a single top-level call, nested different-key leaders compute $\\mu T_{K'}.\\,F_{K'}(T_{\\text{anc}} \\cup \\{K \\mapsto T_K\\}, T_{K'})$ monotonically per outer pass, reaching the joint least fixed point by Bekić's theorem.\n  - **However**, because [`rule-iteration`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2049) streams each newly discovered tuple to the caller continuation `k` *before* the outer pass finishes, `k` executes under the caller's `ctx` (where `call-key` is absent from `::tables`). Whenever `k` evaluates a second call with the **same `call-key`** (for example, `[:find ?x ?y :in $ % :where (path 1 ?x) (path 1 ?y)]` with `left-rules`), the inner [`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2068-L2082) clears `call-key` from the shared `(::hits st)` set, prematurely terminating the outer fixed-point loop and **dropping valid answers** (full trace in **Question 4, D1**).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Vector-Head Stratification Fix (Review P1)\n\n**Closes the vector-head vs. list-head bypass as specified, with one residual malformed-head edge case (Question 4, D3).**\n\n- Changing `(seq? (first %))` to `(sequential? (first %))` in [`check-rules-stratified!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2552) brings both `[(p ?x) ...]` and `[[p ?x] ...]` (including required-bound `[[p [?x] ?y] ...]`) under the pre-evaluation cycle check in [`q-with-state`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2703-L2704) with zero source reads.\n- [`collect-rule-calls`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2524-L2543) accurately mirrors [`emit-clause`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2112-L2127) across `not`, `not-join`, `and`, `or`, and `or-join`, and `reach` follows both positive and negated edges from every negated callee, catching self-negation and arbitrary multi-hop cycles through negation while admitting stratified negation outside the cycle.\n- **Residual gap (D3)**: Because neither [`rule-head`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1953-L1966) nor [`emit-rule`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2093) requires `(sequential? head)`, a non-sequential collection head such as a set `'[[#{p} [1 :e 2] (not (p))]]` still skips `(sequential? (first %))` in `check-rules-stratified!` while evaluating in `emit-rule`/`rule-head` (see **D3**).\n\n---\n\n## 3. E15/E16 Convention Freezes, `cell-same?` Bijection, and Corpus Graduation\n\n**Meets the freeze-via-fixtures discipline, EXCEPT for a factual error in E16's adapter-category description (Question 4, D4).**\n\n- **Corpus and provenance integrity**: Verified all `113` cases (`56` executable, `9` difference, `19` refusal, `29` pending), `28` points, and `12` fixtures across [datomic-q-v1.json](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.json), [datomic-q-v1.provenance.edn](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.provenance.edn#L9-L13), [datomic-q-v1.README.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.README.md#L129-L130), and [`resource-blake3`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc#L95-L100) (`51e021815d94ea0f9e4a9af119590c19af2a7450b20db7c7e918c0a0c7bb128c`). All 14 `rules.*` cases and `agg.non-variable-argument` honestly record `\"evidence\": \"local-dao-source\"` and `\"oracle\": \"pending\"`.\n- **Phase 2 carries resolved cleanly**:\n  - [`cell-same?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc#L322-L332) now enforces a consuming one-to-one matching (exact because numeric-value equality `(zero? (cbor/num-compare a b))` is an equivalence relation on numerics).\n  - [`parse-aggregate`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2374-L2376) (backed by [`check-declared-symbols`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2477-L2481) for bare/`_` symbols) refuses non-variable aggregate arguments statically, and [`validate-clauses!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2192-L2194) + [`clause-bound-vars`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2501) refuse non-flat rule calls cleanly.\n  - E15 ([datomic-q-v1.errata.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L242-L251)) accurately records the two-layer `rand`/`sample` refusal, `(max n ?x)` tie order, and the non-variable aggregate-arg refusal.\n- **Inaccuracy in E16 (D4)**: E16 ([datomic-q-v1.errata.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L117-L119)) claims unbound required-bound rule calls surface through the adapter as `:evaluation-failed`, when in fact both [`classify-core-failure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L579-L583) and [`the-adapter-classifies-rule-refusals`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc#L375-L377) classify them as **`:invalid-request`** (`:cognitect.anomalies/incorrect`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Defects Missed by the Review Chain\n\n1. **P1 | [query.cljc:2066-2083](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2066-L2083) ([`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2057-L2083), [`note-hit`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1969-L1973), [`clear-hit`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1976-L1978)) | Concurrent `rule-fixpoint` leader activations for the same `call-key` clobber (and on `reduced`, leak) `(::hits st)`, losing answers on left-recursive multi-call queries (D1)**\n   - **Evidence / trace**: [`rule-iteration`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2049) invokes `(k st (:acc a2') b')` mid-pass. `k` closes over the caller's `ctx` ([query.cljc:2204-2205](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2204-L2205)), where `call-key` is *not* in `::tables`. On the suite's own `graph` (`1-\u003e2-\u003e3-\u003e1, 3-\u003e4, 5-\u003e6`) and `left-rules`, consider:\n     ```clojure\n     (qq '[:find ?x ?y :in $ % :where (path 1 ?x) (path 1 ?y)] (graph) left-rules)\n     ```\n     Both clauses share `call-key = ['path (binding-key [1 FREE])]`. During Pass 1 of outer `(path 1 ?x)`, Def 1 calls [`read-table`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2001) once before `each-st` (setting `::hits = #{K}`), derives `[1 3]` (`?x = 3`), and streams to `k` (`(path 1 ?y)`). Inner `(path 1 ?y)` sees `table = nil` in outer `ctx`, runs its own `rule-fixpoint` for `K`, and exits at [line 2082](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2082) via `:else [(clear-hit st K) acc']` — **erasing `K` from `(::hits st)`**. Outer Pass 1 finishes with `(:new a2) = [[1 3]]` and `(hit? st K) =\u003e false`, stopping at Pass 1 and silently losing `?x = 1` and `?x = 4` (returning 8 of 16 rows; with recursive-first definition order, stopping at Pass 0 and losing `?x = 3` as well). The same bug hits `(path ?a ?b) (path ?c ?d)` (`K = ['path [FREE FREE]]`) and `(path 1 ?x) (not-join [?x] (path 1 ?z) ...)`. Conversely, [line 2078](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2078) (`stopped? [st (reduced acc')]`) omits `clear-hit`, leaking an inner `exists-st` hit into `st`.\n   - **Why existing tests missed it**: [`a-rule-used-twice-in-one-query-is-independent-per-call`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc#L163-L166) used `(path 1 ?x) (path 5 ?y)` (distinct keys), and [`execution_test.cljc:426`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/dao/space/query/execution_test.cljc#L426) used right-recursive `chain-rules` (which binds `?m` to distinct keys and never needs Pass 1).\n   - **Recommended correction**: Capture `was-hit? (hit? st call-key)` on entry to [`rule-fixpoint`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2066) and restore `(if was-hit? (note-hit st call-key) (clear-hit st call-key))` on both `stopped?` ([line 2078](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2078)) and `:else` ([line 2082](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2082)), leaving `(exec/terminal? st)` untouched (or allocate a unique table-activation ID in `st`). Pin same-key sibling calls `(path 1 ?x) (path 1 ?y)` with `left-rules` (both clause orders) and `(path 1 ?x) (not-join [?x] (path 1 ?z) ...)` in [query_rules_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc).\n\n2. **P2 (Gate Blocker) | [jolt_j2_lane.clj:253-274](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L253-L274) | `dao.space.query-rules-test` is unlisted in the Jolt J2 manifest (D2)**\n   - **Evidence**: Branch `datomic-q-p3-ci` adds portable [query_rules_test.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc) without adding `\"dao.space.query-rules-test\"` to `included` in [jolt_j2_lane.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj). Merging as-is will break [`check-manifest!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L327-L363) on `master` (`J2 manifest FAILED: UNLISTED dao.space.query-rules-test`, sixth recurrence) and omit a pure query suite required by [dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:924-925](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L924-L925).\n   - **Recommended correction**: Add `\"dao.space.query-rules-test\"` to `included` in [jolt_j2_lane.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L256) and run the Jolt single-namespace check before merge.\n\n3. **P2 | [query.cljc:1958-1966, 2093, 2552](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1958-L1966) | Non-sequential rule heads bypass `check-rules-stratified!` or misclassify as `:evaluation-failed` (D3)**\n   - **Evidence**: [`check-rules-stratified!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2552) filters by `(sequential? (first %))`, whereas [`emit-rule`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2093) uses `(first (first %))` and [`rule-head`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1959) uses `(vec (rest head))`. A set head `'[[#{p} [1 :e 2] (not (p))]]` skips `check-rules-stratified!` (`(sequential? #{p}) =\u003e false`) yet evaluates in `emit-rule`/`rule-head` without refusal; a scalar head `'[[123 [1 :e 2]]]` throws raw host `IllegalArgumentException` in `(first (first %))`, surfacing at the adapter as `:evaluation-failed` (`fault`) instead of `:invalid-request` (`incorrect`).\n   - **Recommended correction**: Require `(and (sequential? rule) (sequential? (first rule)) (symbol? (ffirst rule)))` in rule validation / [`rule-head`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L1958) (throwing `ex-info` `\"malformed rule head\"` with `{:head ...}`) so stratification, core evaluation, and adapter `:invalid-request` classification share one exact head grammar.\n\n4. **P2 | [datomic-q-v1.errata.md:117-119](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L117-L119) | E16 misstates the adapter error discriminator for unbound required-bound rule calls (D4)**\n   - **Evidence**: Core throws `(ex-info \"Rule required-bound variable is not bound at the call\" {:rule rule-name, :var ...})` ([query.cljc:2026-2027](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2026-L2027)). Because `(some? (ex-data e))` is true, [`classify-core-failure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L579-L583) maps it to **`:invalid-request`** (`:cognitect.anomalies/incorrect`), pinned at [query_rules_test.cljc:375-377](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/test/dao/space/query_rules_test.cljc#L375-L377) — not `:evaluation-failed` (`:cognitect.anomalies/fault`).\n   - **Recommended correction**: Update E16 to name `:invalid-request` (`:cognitect.anomalies/incorrect`, via the adapter's generic core-`ex-info` refusal path, consistent with unbound fn/`not-join` variables), keeping Datomic's exact category on the Phase 5 oracle measurement list.\n\n5. **P3 | [dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:233](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p3-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L233) | Stale `active-call guard` text in adjacent supported-domain row (D5)**\n   - **Recommended correction**: While editing the branch for D1–D4, update row 233 (`Finite positive recursive rules`) alongside row 232 so it no longer states `\"Current active-call guard is not a completeness proof\"`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Sign-Off Verdict\n\nNOT SIGNED OFF: Fix D1 (`rule-fixpoint` `::hits` preservation across nested same-`call-key` leader activations on both normal and `reduced` exits, with left-recursive same-key conjunction/negation regression tests), D2 (register `\"dao.space.query-rules-test\"` in `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` and verify on Jolt), D3 (reject non-sequential/malformed rule heads uniformly with `ex-info` so stratification cannot be bypassed by set heads and adapter errors stay `:invalid-request`), and D4 (correct `:evaluation-failed` to `:invalid-request` in `datomic-q-v1.errata.md` E16; optionally fold D5 on `dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:233`), then re-verify and return for confirmation and sign-off.\n","duration_seconds":931.680608,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":2367